    "text": "{\n  \"anomaly_detected\": true,\n  \"confidence\": 0.98,\n  \"anomalies\": [\n    {\n      \"category\": \"other\",\n      \"components\": [\"U3\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"U3.10 (BS0)\", \"U3.11 (BS1)\", \"U3.12 (BS2)\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"VCC\", \"GND\"],\n      \"observed\": \"On the DISPLAY sheet, BS0 (pin 10) is tied to VCC, while BS1 (pin 11) and BS2 (pin 12) are tied to GND. This selects BS2:BS1:BS0 = 001 instead of the I2C-mode setting.\",\n      \"expected\": \"For the intended I2C interface, BS0 should be tied to GND, BS1 to VCC, and BS2 to GND (BS2:BS1:BS0 = 010).\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"source\": \"schematic\",\n          \"quote\": \"DISPLAY sheet, page 3: U3 pins 10 (BS0), 11 (BS1), and 12 (BS2) are shown strapped respectively to VCC, GND, and GND.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source\": \"spec\",\n          \"quote\": \"Display ... interface-select pins ... BS0 (pin 10) \u2192 GND; BS1 (pin 11) \u2192 VCC; BS2 (pin 12) \u2192 GND.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The SSD1306 is configured for a parallel interface rather than I2C, so the MCU's two-wire display signals will not operate the display as intended.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.98\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The display interface-selection straps are reversed for BS0 and BS1 compared with the specified I2C configuration. The SSD1306 will therefore select a parallel interface while its data pins are wired for I2C.\"\n}",
